        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF141 File.webkitRelativePath / HTMLInputElement.webkitdirectory]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27178</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27178"/>
        <updated>2025-06-30T01:20:26.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Firefox 141 supports <code class="notranslate">webkitdirectory</code> on android in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1887878" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1887878</a>, which was added in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3161889553" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27108" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27108/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27108">#27108</a></p>
<p dir="auto">What this does is allow you to mark that an input offers a folder selector, and when you select a folder it returns an array of <code class="notranslate">File</code> entries with the path in the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/File/webkitRelativePath" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">File.webkitRelativePath</code></a> property (see <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLInputElement/webkitdirectory#examples" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">HTMLInputElement.webkitdirectory</code></a> for detail).</p>
<p dir="auto">But it turns out that on Firefox for Android the returned <code class="notranslate">webkitRelativePath</code> is always an empty string.<br>
What I think this means is that FF supports <code class="notranslate">webkitRelativePath</code> and <code class="notranslate">HTMLInputElement/webkitdirectory</code> in the sense that they exist as entities, but they are both partial implementations.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/danielhjacobs/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/danielhjacobs">@danielhjacobs</a> Can you please confirm this.</p>
<p dir="auto">I have updated the features appropriately.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3166057685" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40024" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40024/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40024">mdn/content#40024</a></p>]]></content>
